{"packet_id":"D006-01","doc_id":"D006","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"rent_increase_limits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Berkeley Rent Ordinance annual general adjustment 5% cap (Measure BB)","requirement":"A landlord of a fully covered unit may not raise rent by more than the Annual General Adjustment, capped at a maximum of 5%. A landlord may petition for rent increases only for completed capital improvements, not planned ones.","key_value":"maximum 5% Annual General Adjustment","coverage_conditions":"Fully covered rental units under the Berkeley Rent Ordinance; new construction certified after 1980, most single-family homes and most condominiums are only partially covered and have no rent ceiling.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"built","role":"exempt","op":"after","date":"1980","basis":"certificate_of_occupancy"}],"per_tenancy":"Applies to fully covered units; most single-family homes and most condominiums are only partially covered.","coverage_quotes":["Most units in multifamily properties built before 1980","New Construction Units (units with a certificate of occupancy issued after 1980)"]},"exemptions":"Units only partially covered by the Ordinance (for example new construction certified after 1980, most single-family homes, most condominiums); unused banked AGAs may still be used.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"valid_through":null,"citation":"Berkeley Mun. Code ch. 13.76","quoted_span":"The maximum AGA is 5%. This means that, if the formula in the Rent Ordinance results in an AGA that is greater than 5%, the AGA approved by the Board for that year can be no more than 5%.","interaction":"Certain government-subsidized units are only partially covered because federal or state law or regulation prohibits rent control.","relations":[],"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D006-01","doc_id":"D006","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Berkeley Rent Ordinance just cause eviction changes (Measure BB)","requirement":"Tenants in covered units may be evicted only for just cause; nonpayment eviction requires rental debt of at least one month's Fair Market Rent; failure to sign a similar lease is not cause; the Rent Board must annually adjust owner move-in relocation assistance.","key_value":"at least 1 month's Fair Market Rent","coverage_conditions":"Tenants in units fully or partially covered by the Berkeley Rent Ordinance.","applicability":{"conditions":[],"per_tenancy":"Units where the tenant shares a kitchen or bath with a landlord who lived on the same property at the start of the tenancy are exempt from the Ordinance.","coverage_quotes":[]},"exemptions":"Rental units where the tenant shares kitchen or bath facilities with the landlord are exempt only if the landlord lived on the property before the tenant.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"valid_through":null,"citation":"Berkeley Mun. Code ch. 13.76","quoted_span":"For a landlord to evict a tenant for nonpayment of rent, the tenant must owe an amount of rental debt equal to or greater than one month of the Fair Market Rent (FMR) value for a unit of equivalent size in the metro area Oakland-Fremont, CA HUD Metro FMR as determined by the US Department of Housing and Urban Development for the fiscal year in which the rent is demanded.","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
